  "challenge": "This is decidable as REJECT without a human. Policy for TM-003 explicitly frames a due date on/before the invoice date as a coercion tactic, and here the due date equals the invoice date while the body still claims Net 30 (TM-001 confirms a 30-day miss)—a direct terms contradiction, not an ambiguity needing vendor clarification. Gadgets Co. is an active contracted Net-30 vendor, unit price matches the GadgetX reference exactly ($750), and there are no PO/references on the invoice; combined with IN-003 (20 units vs standing stock of 5), fulfillment is impossible as billed. PO-001’s manager-approval path applies to otherwise-valid over-threshold invoices, not ones that already fail the coercion and stock checks, so the packet supports rejection rather than escalation.",
  "proposed_outcome": "REJECT",
  "cites_finding_codes": ["TM-003", "TM-001", "IN-003", "PO-001"]
}
